~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] How to read the report below
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  'Baseline R2' is the real model (0.76). 'Random R2' is what the same model achieves when
  potencies are shuffled         (-0.01 on average over 100 shuffles). The Z-score counts how many
  standard deviations the real         result sits above the shuffled results; the pass criterion
  used here is real R2 > mean + 2.33 SD (~99% confidence).
  If the verdict is PASSED, the predictive signal is not a chance correlation. Note that this test
  uses Morgan         fingerprints and the most frequently selected stacking architecture from
  step 01.
